# Agent Wallet Bench

Coding agents set up crypto wallets and use them on their own. Each square is one agent with one wallet; its link opens the run shown in that square.

Each square shows the newest run for that agent and wallet, with its checks in order. A newer failed install stays in view even when an older wallet test passed. Unclear, not recorded, not run and not applicable are each told apart from a failed check. Payment tests have five checks. Earlier runs and comparisons between sets are on the pair's page. The filters work the same here, on the page and as JSON.
<%= for {key, selected} <- @matrix.filters, selected != "", option <- @matrix.options[key], option.id == selected do %>
- <%= key %> filter: <%= line(option.label) %><% end %>
<%= for grid <- @matrix.grids do %>
## <%= grid_title(grid.grid) %>

<%= grid.tested %> of <%= grid.total %> squares have results; <%= grid.never_run %> never run.

<%= grid_table(@matrix, grid) %>
<% end %>
[How the bench works](/wallet-bench/how-it-works): the checks, what each result means, and how Techtree runs each test.
<%= trailer() %>
